;; collections.corpus -- collection TYPES mova lacks entirely: array-map
;; (with 1.13's raised keyword-key growth threshold -- an array-map with 9
;; keyword keys stays a PersistentArrayMap in real Clojure 1.13, where
;; older Clojure would have promoted it to a hash-map), and
;; clojure.lang.PersistentQueue. Also transient-collection semantics:
;; disj!/dissoc!/pop!, reuse of a transient AFTER persistent! (Clojure
;; throws IllegalAccessError; mova silently keeps mutating it), and
;; transient on a type that doesn't support it (Clojure throws
;; ClassCastException; mova silently hands back the original collection
;; unchanged). All forms self-contained (no cross-form session state).
;;
;; compat/s4-sorted-vecof (2026-08-20): sorted-map/-by, sorted-set/-by,
;; subseq, rsubseq, rseq, sorted?, and vector-of all now conform -- moved
;; to tests/conformance/corpus/sorted-colls.corpus.
;;
;; compat/c10-datastructures (2026-08-21): clojure.lang.PersistentQueue
;; (Value::Queue, a Rust-native FIFO) and `set?` on a sorted-set now
;; conform -- both moved to tests/conformance/corpus/collections.corpus.

;; -- array-map, 1.13 keyword-key threshold --
;; C2 (defstruct): `array-map` itself now exists in mova (added alongside
;; struct-maps -- the vendored data_structures.clj's own struct-vs-other-
;; map-classes `are` test calls it directly), but mova's `class`/`type`
;; still reports it via the generic `m.len() <= 8` size threshold
;; (`types::builtin_class_name`), not "real array-map, stays
;; PersistentArrayMap regardless of size" -- so `(type ...)` on a 9-key
;; array-map STILL diverges (mova says PersistentHashMap, oracle says
;; PersistentArrayMap). `(count ...)` on the very same form now conforms
;; (promoted to tests/conformance/corpus/collections.corpus).
(type (array-map :a 1 :b 2 :c 3 :d 4 :e 5 :f 6 :g 7 :h 8 :i 9))

;; -- transients: missing ops -- ALL PROMOTED (W3d): `pop!`/`dissoc!`/
;; `disj!` now exist in core.mova, aliased to their persistent
;; counterparts like `conj!`/`assoc!` before them; the three forms moved
;; to corpus/collections.corpus's tail.

;; -- transients: silent wrongness --
(let [t (transient [1 2 3])] (persistent! t) (conj! t 4))
(transient (list 1 2 3))
(transient (range 5))

;; -- S7 (MapEntry branch, found while closing clojure_walk.clj) --
;; `builtins/predicates.rs`'s `coll?`/`map?`/`set?`/`seqable?` were never
;; extended to S4's sorted/typed collection variants, even though
;; `types.rs`'s OWN `is_coll`/`is_map`/`is_set` (which back `instance?
;; clojure.lang.IPersistentCollection` etc) were -- so the two registries
;; disagree with each other and with the oracle. This is what the last 4
;; failing assertions of `tests/clojure-suite/vendor/clojure_walk.clj`'s
;; `walk` deftest are: `clojure/walk.clj`'s `(coll? form)` branch is never
;; taken for a sorted map/set, so `walk` falls to `:else (outer form)` and
;; never applies `inner` (measured: 6 where the oracle gives 9, 60 where it
;; gives 63). Unrelated to MapEntry -- entered here rather than fixed in
;; that branch so its bench/suite evidence stays attributable.
